# Under Pressure Custom Apparel — Cloudflare Pages _redirects
# Place this file in customer-site/ (repo root for this Pages project)

# ── Root URL serves the store ────────────────────────────────────────
/                /customer-index.html              200
/store           /customer-index.html              200

# ── Dynamic team stores ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: Do NOT add a /team-store rule here, and do NOT add a
# /customer-index rule targeting /customer-index.html either — both
# hit the same trap: Cloudflare Pages automatically strips the .html
# extension off any served HTML file's canonical URL, so a rule whose
# source path equals its own target's clean form creates an infinite
# redirect loop (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS), not a working page. Team
# stores are already served at the clean path /team-store
# automatically. The homepage is the bare domain (/) or /store.
# Every admin-created store still works at:
#   underpressurecustomapparel.com/team-store?team=<subdomain>

# ── Legacy named routes (kept for old links) ─────────────────────────
/rampage         /team-store?team=rampage          200
/rome            /team-store?team=rome             200

# ── Short store URLs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# underpressurecustomapparel.com/<subdomain> for any store, e.g.
# underpressurecustomapparel.com/thefamilystore. Rules above take
# precedence (first match wins), and any actual static file at that
# path (images, .b64 mockups, etc.) is always served before this is
# ever considered — Cloudflare only falls through to _redirects when
# no static asset matches the request path.
/:team           /team-store?team=:team            200
